(5058715, 738302, 22301, '<td valign="top">very blue, very <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=48228" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">sherpet</a> <br/>I have seen this presentation before and you do it well, but I think maybe you should try some new angles then straight ahead. Just my opinion of course, there is something to be learned from keeping a them and experimenting inside that mold, but changing it up completely can be fun too. :)</td>', 'very blue, very  sherpet I have seen this presentation before and you do it well, but I think maybe you should try some new angles then straight ahead. Just my opinion of course, there is something to be learned from keeping a them and experimenting inside that mold, but changing it up completely can be fun too. :)', '2008-11-12 03:19:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5058717, 737114, 22301, '<td valign="top">I don''t see much blue. I think a different angle of the lid would have helped with the composition, also using a tripod or bag to set your camera on would allow you to set up table lamps which would make it the lighting less harsh.</td>', 'I don''t see much blue. I think a different angle of the lid would have helped with the composition, also using a tripod or bag to set your camera on would allow you to set up table lamps which would make it the lighting less harsh.', '2008-11-12 03:22:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5058718, 737663, 22301, '<td valign="top">you shold try using Save for the Web in PS. Here is a little <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tutorial</a>, it will strip the exif data and allow you to get the most detail for your image.</td>', 'you shold try using Save for the Web in PS. Here is a little tutorial, it will strip the exif data and allow you to get the most detail for your image.', '2008-11-12 03:24:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5058719, 738593, 22301, '<td valign="top">I see a little blue but not much, but the overhead composition hurts this photo.</td>', 'I see a little blue but not much, but the overhead composition hurts this photo.', '2008-11-12 03:27:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5058720, 738030, 22301, '<td valign="top">I think more could be done with this object. Yes it is blue, so it meets the challenge but I think you could try and take it further. Where is this usually? Could it you have shot it with the focus on the snowman as it sits in your home? Could it have been placed in a fictitious  scene you created? By itself with a black background and floating in there, it is not too interesting for me to score high marks.</td>', 'I think more could be done with this object. Yes it is blue, so it meets the challenge but I think you could try and take it further. Where is this usually? Could it you have shot it with the focus on the snowman as it sits in your home? Could it have been placed in a fictitious  scene you created? By itself with a black background and floating in there, it is not too interesting for me to score high marks.', '2008-11-12 03:32:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5058721, 738537, 22301, '<td valign="top">I am guessing you put this in the wrong challenge...<br/>You should take a look at this <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tutorial</a> for getting images ready for challenges if you have photoshop. Using the the Save for Web feature will allow you to get the most detail you can.</td>', 'I am guessing you put this in the wrong challenge...You should take a look at this tutorial for getting images ready for challenges if you have photoshop. Using the the Save for Web feature will allow you to get the most detail you can.', '2008-11-12 03:34:56.000000', NULL, 1),
