(5058821, 737998, 60173, '<td valign="top">This is one of those thought provoking shots that does pretty horribly here, heh. I love the colors. There''s just enough that''s recognizable to make this a bit dreamy. I think it definitely has its place, but don''t be upset if it doesn''t score well here.</td>', 'This is one of those thought provoking shots that does pretty horribly here, heh. I love the colors. There''s just enough that''s recognizable to make this a bit dreamy. I think it definitely has its place, but don''t be upset if it doesn''t score well here.', '2008-11-12 05:37:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5058832, 738669, 60173, '<td valign="top">That almost doesn''t look like it''s her own foot! Ohm nom, nom, nom!<br/> <br/>I think the DOF could have been a bit wider to capture both eyes, but the one that caught the focus is darn near spot on. I do love how soft the chosen aperture left the remainder of the photo. The skin tone and lighting are great.<br/> <br/>As for the psychological aspect, I realize Amelia is a girl, but we''re brainwashed to associate blue with boys. I wonder if that is going to have any effect on the votes. I''m probably just thinking about it too hard, heh.</td>', 'That almost doesn''t look like it''s her own foot! Ohm nom, nom, nom! I think the DOF could have been a bit wider to capture both eyes, but the one that caught the focus is darn near spot on. I do love how soft the chosen aperture left the remainder of the photo. The skin tone and lighting are great. As for the psychological aspect, I realize Amelia is a girl, but we''re brainwashed to associate blue with boys. I wonder if that is going to have any effect on the votes. I''m probably just thinking about it too hard, heh.', '2008-11-12 05:51:31.000000', NULL, 1),
