(5070980, 738595, 42013, '<td valign="top">Congrats Steve! Fine shot. Must have been dark when you shot this judging by the 129s exposure.</td>', 'Congrats Steve! Fine shot. Must have been dark when you shot this judging by the 129s exposure.', '2008-11-19 02:14:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5071010, 737889, 74588, '<td valign="top">great</td>', 'great', '2008-11-19 02:18:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5071113, 737581, 93636, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone - any thoughts on how you''d light it more "interestingly", though?<br/> <br/>I went for direct overhead to avoid shadows, so I guess the idea would be to go for a main (or is the correct term "key") light from one side and some fill from the other to get rid of the shadows. Is that right?<br/> <br/>I have an Olympus FL36R, so I really <b>must</b> figure out how to get it off-camera. Anyone with an FZ50 reading and done this?<br/> <br/>Thanks again,<br/>Paul.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone - any thoughts on how you''d light it more "interestingly", though? I went for direct overhead to avoid shadows, so I guess the idea would be to go for a main (or is the correct term "key") light from one side and some fill from the other to get rid of the shadows. Is that right? I have an Olympus FL36R, so I really must figure out how to get it off-camera. Anyone with an FZ50 reading and done this? Thanks again,Paul.', '2008-11-19 02:36:39.000000', NULL, 0),
