(5071722, 738511, 79720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ucanoe:</b></div><hr/><i> how did you do this in basic? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yeah, I thought someone might ask this....the link is in the description, if you''re still interested. Long story short: use a hue/sat layer and desat every channel but the one(s) you want to keep. Make sure that adjustment layer is in normal blend!<br/>....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-12-28 14:22:28.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by ucanoe: how did you do this in basic?  Yeah, I thought someone might ask this....the link is in the description, if you''re still interested. Long story short: use a hue/sat layer and desat every channel but the one(s) you want to keep. Make sure that adjustment layer is in normal blend!....', '2008-11-19 06:58:49.000000', '2008-12-28 14:22:28.000000', 0),
